# p_d4e8 — Jacket Draped at the Armchair in the Afternoon; Tablet at the Counter (fork of p_5d8b)

This fork of p_5d8b addresses two weak spots. First, the jacket-at-chair_k1 evening claim (17:00–23:00) has 1 for and 10 against. The worst-objects log reveals the jacket found at armchair_l1 on day 13 at 15:00 (twice), a location no existing document covers. The jacket's most common location is entry_hook_e1 (6/11 days), but during the afternoon (14:00–17:00) when Mara is home and relaxing, she drapes it over the armchair in the living room. Second, the tablet-at-coffee_table claim (weekday 9–14h) has 1 for and 8 against. The per-object stats show the tablet at counter_k1 on 10/16 sighted days — the counter is its true home during work hours.

What changed from p_5d8b: (1) The jacket gains a new "both 14–17h at armchair_l1, sometimes" block for the afternoon draping. The base entry_hook block is retained. (2) The tablet's base changes from coffee_table_l1 to counter_k1. (3) The wallet-at-chair_k2 evening block is retained (2 for, 9 against — weak but not yet refuted). (4) The tablet claim now tests the counter.

What sets this apart from p_5d8b: at 15:00, the jacket is at the armchair (not the entry hook, not chair_k1); at 11:00 on a weekday, the tablet is at the counter (not the coffee table). What would refute it: the jacket found at the entry hook at 15:00 on most days, or the tablet found at the coffee table at 11:00 consistently.

